.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt PAZARI-AGENT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pazari-agent
.Nd guest memory agent for pazari
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar file
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar file
.Cm panic-open
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar file
.Cm preflight
.Nm
.Cm example-config
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs inside a virtual machine and manages the memory of one workload cgroup.
It throttles the workload with
.Va memory.high
before it reaches
.Va memory.max ,
asks
.Xr pazarid 1
on the host for more memory when the throttle engages, and offers memory back
when the workload no longer needs it.
.Pp
The agent owns
.Va memory.high
and
.Va memory.max
on the workload cgroup.
Nothing else in the guest should write them.
The agent does not start or stop the workload.
.Pp
With no command,
.Nm
runs in the foreground until it receives
.Dv SIGTERM
or
.Dv SIGINT .
It reads its configuration once, at startup.
.Ss The brake
With
.Va P
the guest's
.Va MemTotal ,
the agent sets:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
memory.max  = P - service_reserve
memory.high = memory.max - burst_reserve
.Ed
.Pp
The space between the two limits is the burst reserve.
When the workload reaches
.Va memory.high ,
the kernel throttles its allocations and the agent requests more memory.
The workload continues into the reserve at the throttled rate until the memory
arrives, and the agent then recomputes both limits.
.Pp
.Va memory.high
is raised to
.Va memory.max
only when the guest has reached its ceiling and the exhaustion policy gives up;
see
.Sx Exhaustion .
Sizing the two reserves is covered in
.Xr pazari-agent.toml 5 .
.Ss Modes
The agent is always in one of five modes, reported by the
.Va pazari_agent_mode
metric.
.Bl -tag -width "awaiting_grant"
.It Cm steady
The limits are in place and nothing is pending.
This is the only mode in which the agent accepts a reclaim request from the
host.
.It Cm awaiting_grant
A grant request is outstanding, a refused request is waiting to be retried, or
granted memory has not yet arrived.
The limits do not move.
.It Cm reclaiming
The agent is reclaiming from the workload cgroup before asking the host.
.It Cm releasing
The agent is reclaiming memory from the workload cgroup to return to the host.
.It Cm exhausted
The guest has reached its ceiling.
.El
.Ss Throttles
When the workload throttles at
.Va memory.high ,
the agent asks the host for more.
With
.Cm engine.throttle
set to
.Cm reclaim ,
it first reclaims
.Cm amount
from the workload cgroup, if the guest has that much to spare.
It asks the host only if the reclaim falls short.
.Ss Growing
A grant request asks for the larger of the step the
.Cm engine.grow
strategy names and the workload's current shortfall.
The target is rounded up to the guest's memory block size and capped at the
ceiling the host has set.
.Pp
After a grant, the agent waits for
.Va MemTotal
to reach the target, or for
.Cm settle_grace
to pass, whichever is first, and then works with whatever memory the guest has.
.Pp
A refusal with reason
.Cm ceiling
makes the agent exhausted.
Any other refusal is retried after the delay the host names, or after
.Cm deny_backoff
if it names none.
Such retries continue for as long as the guest is below its ceiling, and the
workload stays throttled while they do.
.Ss Releasing
The
.Cm engine.release
strategy decides when to release and how much.
The agent never releases memory the guest booted with.
.Ss Host reclaim requests
The host may ask the guest to return memory.
The agent refuses outright in any mode other than
.Cm steady .
In
.Cm steady
it returns the smallest of: the amount asked for, the memory plugged above boot
size, and
.Va MemAvailable
less both reserves, rounded down to a memory block.
If that is zero, it refuses.
Otherwise it reclaims the memory as for a release and offers it back.
An accepted request can still fail if the reclaim frees nothing or the workload
is throttled before it finishes; the host is told either way.
.Ss Exhaustion
The agent becomes exhausted when the host refuses a request with reason
.Cm ceiling ,
or when the guest already holds its whole ceiling.
What happens next is set by
.Cm engine.exhaustion
in
.Xr pazari-agent.toml 5 :
.Bl -tag -width "stall"
.It Cm stall
The brake stays on and the workload runs throttled.
The agent keeps retrying for the configured timeout.
If no memory has arrived by then, it raises
.Va memory.high
to
.Va memory.max
and stops retrying; the kernel's OOM killer then acts in the cgroup once the
workload reaches
.Va memory.max .
.It Cm kill
The agent raises
.Va memory.high
to
.Va memory.max
immediately.
Because the agent sets
.Va memory.oom.group
in this mode, the kernel kills the whole cgroup at
.Va memory.max
rather than a single process.
.El
.Pp
The agent leaves
.Cm exhausted ,
and puts the brake back on, when:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
the host raises the ceiling;
.It
.Va MemTotal
rises for any reason;
.It
the workload stays calm for
.Cm engine.recovery_intervals
ticks;
.It
the connection to the host is re-established; or
.It
during a stall, a retry finds room under the ceiling.
.El
.Pp
After a stall has timed out, the agent no longer retries, so only the first four
apply.
.Ss Connection to the host
The agent connects to
.Xr pazarid 1
over the transport in its configuration and reconnects with exponential backoff
if the connection drops.
Neither side keeps state across a connection.
While disconnected, the agent leaves the limits where they are.
.Ss Shutdown
On
.Dv SIGTERM
or
.Dv SIGINT ,
the agent sets
.Va memory.high
to
.Cm max
and exits, so the workload is not left throttled.
If the agent is killed it cannot do this; run
.Cm panic-open
from
.Va ExecStopPost
to cover that case.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar file , Fl -config Ar file
Read the configuration from
.Ar file
instead of
.Pa /etc/pazari/agent.toml .
May appear before or after a command.
.It Fl -version
Print the version and exit.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print usage and exit.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm panic-open
Set
.Va memory.high
on the workload cgroup to
.Cm max
and exit.
Intended for
.Va ExecStopPost ,
which runs after every exit of the agent, including when it is killed.
.It Cm preflight
Run the startup checks, print the results, and exit.
See
.Sx PREFLIGHT .
.It Cm example-config
Print an annotated configuration file with every key at its default.
.El
.Sh PREFLIGHT
The agent runs the following checks at startup and refuses to start if any of
them fails.
Warnings do not prevent startup.
Results are printed as
.Ql Ar severity Ar name : Ar detail ,
where
.Ar severity
is
.Cm pass ,
.Cm warn
or
.Cm fail .
.Bl -tag -width "transparent hugepages"
.It Cm cgroup v2
The unified cgroup hierarchy is mounted.
.It Cm workload cgroup
.Cm runtime.cgroup
exists and the agent can read and write the files it needs.
A failure lists each file it could not use.
.It Cm agent cgroup
The agent is not inside the workload cgroup.
Warns instead of failing if it cannot tell, as inside a cgroup namespace.
.It Cm memory controller
The memory controller is enabled for the workload cgroup.
.It Cm auto-onlining
The kernel onlines hot-plugged memory automatically.
Without this, plugged memory never becomes usable.
Warns unless it is onlined movable, since otherwise it cannot reliably be
unplugged.
Write
.Cm online_movable
to
.Pa /sys/devices/system/memory/auto_online_blocks ,
or boot with
.Va memhp_default_state=online_movable .
.It Cm transparent hugepages
Transparent hugepages are not set to
.Cm always .
Fails by default; see
.Cm runtime.thp_always_fatal
in
.Xr pazari-agent.toml 5 .
.It Cm block size
.Pa /sys/devices/system/memory/block_size_bytes
is readable and non-zero.
.It Cm balloon
The guest has no virtio-balloon device.
Warns if a virtio device cannot be identified.
.It Cm swap
The guest has swap and the workload cgroup may use it.
Only ever a warning, and skipped when
.Cm engine.reclaim_swappiness
is 0.
.El
.Pp
At startup, but not under
.Cm preflight ,
the agent also refuses to start unless
.Va MemTotal
is at least
.Cm service_reserve
plus
.Cm burst_reserve
plus one memory block.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev RUST_LOG
Log filter, in
.Va tracing-subscriber
.Va EnvFilter
syntax.
Defaults to
.Cm info .
.It Ev JOURNAL_STREAM
Set by systemd.
When it refers to the agent's standard error, the agent logs to the journal
directly, with structured fields prefixed
.Cm F_ .
.It Ev NOTIFY_SOCKET
Set by systemd for
.Va Type=notify .
The agent reports readiness and sends watchdog pings here.
.It Ev WATCHDOG_USEC
Watchdog interval.
The agent pings at half this interval.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/pazari/agent.toml
Default configuration file; see
.Xr pazari-agent.toml 5 .
.It Pa <cgroup>/memory.high , <cgroup>/memory.max
Written by the agent.
Under the
.Cm systemd
backend, set through the unit instead.
.It Pa <cgroup>/memory.oom.group
Set at startup: to 1 under
.Cm kind = Qq kill ,
to 0 otherwise.
.It Pa <cgroup>/memory.reclaim
Written to free memory before it is returned to the host, and to make room on a
throttle.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
.Cm preflight
exits 1 if any check failed and 0 otherwise.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check a guest before deploying the agent:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ pazari-agent preflight
.Ed
.Pp
Generate a configuration file to edit:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# pazari-agent example-config > /etc/pazari/agent.toml
.Ed
.Pp
A systemd unit for the agent is given in
.Xr pazari 7 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pazari-stress 1 ,
.Xr pazarid 1 ,
.Xr pazari-agent.toml 5 ,
.Xr cgroups 7 ,
.Xr pazari 7
